WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:17.756
"What's going on?" someone shouted.

2
00:00:17.757 --> 00:00:21.432
"My car just stopped!" the mayor exclaimed.

3
00:00:21.433 --> 00:00:25.990
Several people rushed toward the mayor's car, including Mr. Newman.

4
00:00:25.991 --> 00:00:29.461
After a moment Mr. Newman let out a shout.

5
00:00:29.462 --> 00:00:33.042
"The car is out of gas," he announced.

6
00:00:33.043 --> 00:00:39.467
The mayor frowned. "You said you filled it before you dropped it off at the parking lot last night."

7
00:00:39.468 --> 00:00:43.019
"I did." Mr. Newman looked perplexed.

8
00:00:43.020 --> 00:00:46.656
"Maybe there's a hole in the gas tank," someone called out.

9
00:00:46.657 --> 00:00:49.010
More people gathered around the car.

10
00:00:49.011 --> 00:00:52.258
Henry and his friends watched from their float.

11
00:00:52.259 --> 00:00:57.645
"Uh-oh," Maggie blurted out. "It looks like that threat is coming true!"

12
00:00:57.646 --> 00:01:01.824
"The car was parked at the high school all night," Cole said.

13
00:01:01.825 --> 00:01:06.034
"Someone could have sneaked in and drained most of the gas.

14
00:01:06.035 --> 00:01:10.431
That way the car would stall after a few minutes."

15
00:01:10.432 --> 00:01:14.279
"And mess up the parade," Henry finished.

16
00:01:14.280 --> 00:01:19.465
"That's exactly what I was thinking. But who could have done that?"

17
00:01:19.466 --> 00:01:22.751
"What about Jackson?" Cole suggested.

18
00:01:22.752 --> 00:01:27.300
"He knew all about the parade plans because of his newspaper story.

19
00:01:27.301 --> 00:01:31.986
So he probably knew the mayor's car was parked at the high school."

20
00:01:31.987 --> 00:01:34.228
"Mr. Newman knew too."

21
00:01:34.229 --> 00:01:39.336
Maggie shot a look at the auto shop owner, who was under the car, checking the gas tank.

22
00:01:39.337 --> 00:01:42.780
"Maybe he didn't really fill the mayor's gas tank."

23
00:01:42.781 --> 00:01:49.128
"But Mr. Newman doesn't have a motive for ruining the parade," Henry reminded her.

24
00:01:49.129 --> 00:01:54.131
"I know someone who has a motive." Maggie pointed toward the shops.

25
00:01:54.132 --> 00:01:57.346
"We're stopped right in front of Miss Bishop's store.

26
00:01:57.347 --> 00:02:02.530
Maybe that was her plan all along—to get people to notice her store!"

27
00:02:02.531 --> 00:02:06.707
"Maybe," Cole said. Then he grinned.

28
00:02:06.708 --> 00:02:12.935
"But I can't imagine Miss Bishop getting her hands dirty by draining gas from a tank!"

29
00:02:12.936 --> 00:02:17.385
"Why not?" Maggie challenged him. "Because she's a woman?

30
00:02:17.386 --> 00:02:20.790
Lots of girls and women know how to drain gas."

31
00:02:20.791 --> 00:02:26.410
Cole shrugged. "That's true. I'm just not sure Miss Bishop is one of them.

32
00:02:26.411 --> 00:02:29.221
She wouldn't want to mess up her manicure."

33
00:02:29.222 --> 00:02:33.376
Henry gasped. "That's it!"

34
00:02:33.377 --> 00:02:37.881
"What?" Cole asked. "Is Miss Bishop the culprit?"

35
00:02:37.882 --> 00:02:43.116
"No, but I'm pretty sure I know who is."

36
00:02:43.117 --> 00:02:49.400
Henry peered into the watching crowd, and then smiled. "Come with me!"

37
00:02:49.401 --> 00:02:53.727
He jumped down from the float and led his friends toward Snake and his band.

38
00:02:53.728 --> 00:02:59.142
The band was watching from the sidewalk as Mr. Newman and others checked the mayor's car.

39
00:02:59.143 --> 00:03:01.823
Maggie gasped when she saw them.

40
00:03:01.824 --> 00:03:06.787
"It was Snake, wasn't it?" she whispered. "I knew it!"

41
00:03:06.788 --> 00:03:11.576
"No, it wasn't Snake." Henry stopped in front of the band.

42
00:03:11.577 --> 00:03:15.269
"Hi, guys. Jade, can I talk to you?"

43
00:03:15.270 --> 00:03:18.658
"What is it?" Jade sounded sullen.

44
00:03:18.659 --> 00:03:24.051
Henry took a deep breath. "You did it, didn't you?" he said.

45
00:03:24.052 --> 00:03:28.984
"You left that threat on the website, and you emptied the gas tank."

46
00:03:28.985 --> 00:03:33.176
Jade gasped. "How did you know?" she blurted out.

47
00:03:33.177 --> 00:03:35.344
Then she covered her mouth.

48
00:03:35.345 --> 00:03:39.417
"Um, I mean, I don't know what you're talking about!"

49
00:03:39.418 --> 00:03:43.092
Snake and the other band members looked confused.

50
00:03:43.093 --> 00:03:49.281
"What's going on?" Snake asked. "Jade, what's the Lemonade Kid talking about?"

51
00:03:49.282 --> 00:03:52.744
"Nothing," Jade muttered, glaring at Henry.

52
00:03:52.745 --> 00:03:58.227
"So Jade is our culprit?" Cole said. "How'd you know that, Henry?"

53
00:03:58.228 --> 00:04:04.066
"It was what Maggie said about girls being able to drain gas," Henry said.

54
00:04:04.067 --> 00:04:08.929
"That's when I remembered that Jade works at her father's garage.

55
00:04:08.930 --> 00:04:12.926
So she probably knows all about stuff like that.

56
00:04:12.927 --> 00:04:17.062
I also remembered that Mr. Newman is pretty strict.

57
00:04:17.063 --> 00:04:22.126
So I figured Jade was the band member who got grounded for being late."

58
00:04:22.127 --> 00:04:27.668
"Yeah, so what?" Eddie said. "That doesn't prove anything."

59
00:04:27.669 --> 00:04:31.870
Snake nodded. "It wasn't Jade's fault she got grounded.

60
00:04:31.871 --> 00:04:34.627
We talked her into staying late."

61
00:04:34.628 --> 00:04:36.926
"Okay," Henry said.

62
00:04:36.927 --> 00:04:42.241
"But I think she still felt guilty about making the band drop out of the parade.

63
00:04:42.242 --> 00:04:45.449
So she left that threat on the website.

64
00:04:45.450 --> 00:04:50.533
Then she messed with the mayor's car to try to ruin the parade."

65
00:04:50.534 --> 00:04:57.607
"I'm sorry!" Jade burst into tears. "I was just mad, that's all.

66
00:04:57.608 --> 00:05:03.759
I was only ten minutes late to work! Why does my dad have to be so strict?"

67
00:05:03.760 --> 00:05:05.597
Snake stared at her.

68
00:05:05.598 --> 00:05:12.506
"So you did this?" He waved a hand toward the mayor's car. "Not cool, Jade."

69
00:05:12.507 --> 00:05:15.405
"I know." Jade sniffled.

70
00:05:15.406 --> 00:05:19.197
"You've got to tell the mayor you did it," Henry said.

71
00:05:19.198 --> 00:05:22.592
"Otherwise he might blame your dad."

72
00:05:22.593 --> 00:05:33.073
Jade sniffled again. "Okay," she mumbled. "I'll go confess right now."

73
00:05:33.074 --> 00:05:40.673
Soon someone brought more gas for the mayor's car, and the parade continued.

74
00:05:40.674 --> 00:05:46.957
In the end Mrs. Sweet won the mayor's prize, and Miss Bishop won the popular vote.

75
00:05:46.958 --> 00:05:52.251
Henry thought Maggie might be mad that The Lemonade Detectives hadn't won either prize.

76
00:05:52.252 --> 00:05:54.227
But Maggie didn't mind a bit.

77
00:05:54.228 --> 00:05:59.625
Because The Lemonade Detectives still got interviewed on TV.

78
00:05:59.626 --> 00:06:10.764
They were the kid detectives who'd solved the parade mystery!
